  "customHelp": "CHRONICLE TCG — PLAYTEST CONFIGURATION\n\nDECK CONSTRUCTION\nMain Deck: 25-30 cards, maximum 2 copies of a card.\nTitan Deck: 1-5 Titan cards, maximum 2 copies of a card.\nResource Deck: exactly 15 Resource cards. Resources are exempt from the normal 2-copy limit.\n\nTCG ARENA SETUP\nTitan cards are automatically separated into the visible Titan Deck.\nResource cards are automatically separated into the hidden Resource Deck.\nAll other cards remain in the Main Deck.\n\nGAME START\nDraw 5 cards from the Main Deck. No mulligan. Start with 3 Points.\nThe first player skips both draws on their first turn.\nThe SECOND player should manually draw 1 Main Deck card and 1 Resource card on their first turn.\n\nTURN: DP > SP > MP > BP > EP\nOn later turns, draw 1 Main Deck card and 1 Resource.\nResources drawn from the Resource Deck go into the normal Hand.\nThere is NO separate Resource Zone.\n\nPLAY AREA LAYOUT\nLeft: Titan Deck.\nCenter: Field Spell Zone, Titan Creature Zone, and Creature Zones C1-C3.\nRight: Resource Deck above Main Deck.\nBottom: Spell Stack.\nThere is NO Graveyard zone displayed on the playmat.\n\nTitan Deck is public/visible and can be checked at any time.\nMain Deck contains normal Creatures and Spells.\n\nMANUAL RULES\nPlayers enforce Stage Boost requirements, one Creature played from Hand per turn,\nResource attachment, Spell costs/timing, combat, Field Spell replacement,\ndirect attacks, Points, hand limit, and deck-out.",
